 \ReviewerComment{L979-982: It is better to use hourly ERA5 data and still forecast at 6h lead time. This way, you will have more data to train and validate the model.}
 
-\PendingResponse
+\AuthorResponse{We thank the reviewer for this suggestion. It combines two changes, hourly rather than six-hourly inputs and hourly issue times that increase the number of training samples, and we tested both in reduced-period experiments. Hourly ERA5 box means were built for 2017--2021 and reproduce the six-hourly regional series at 00/06/12/18~UTC. XGBoost and BiLSTM-Attention were refitted with five seeds in four configurations: six-hourly or hourly inputs over the same 30-h history, each with training issue times either at 00/06/12/18~UTC (A and B; 4,374 samples) or every hour (CA and CB; 26,244 samples). The validation and test targets (2020 and 2021), the final-hour target $(t_0+5\,\mathrm{h},t_0+6\,\mathrm{h}]$ and the 6-h lead time were identical. Relative to A, the configuration proposed by the reviewer (CB) changed overall test RMSE by $-1.57\%$ for XGBoost and $-1.86\%$ for BiLSTM-Attention; neither change was robust, because the moving-block intervals included zero. In the exploratory decomposition, most of the change was associated with hourly issue times (CA versus A: $-0.92\%$ and $-1.89\%$) rather than with hourly inputs. Wet and upper-tail RMSE were 2.3--6.0\% lower for CB than for A in all five seeds of both models, but these subset results are exploratory and unadjusted for multiplicity. The second experiment was designed after the first comparison had been seen, the evaluation uses one test year and two models, the hourly training samples are highly autocorrelated, and each epoch contained about six times as many optimization steps. We therefore report these results as motivating further evaluation of hourly data over the full period, not as an established improvement. They are described in Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:limitations} and Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r3hourly_ab} and~\ref{supp-stab:r3hourly_runs}.}
 
-\ChangeLocation
+\ManuscriptChange{Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:limitations} (Limitations and Future Work): new paragraph after the existing six-hour subsampling limitation, which is unchanged. Supplementary Material: new final section ``Hourly input sensitivity'' with Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r3hourly_ab} (configurations A, B, CA and CB for XGBoost and BiLSTM-Attention; primary comparison CB$-$A and exploratory comparisons; all/wet/upper-tail RMSE with seed-t and moving-block intervals) and~\ref{supp-stab:r3hourly_runs} (training samples, epochs and recorded times). Main-study models, splits and results are unchanged; no new training was performed for this revision. Final page and line numbers pending full-manuscript assembly.}
